<title>SWEDEN: Sweden's BTL air freight unit buys German firm.</title>
<headline>Sweden's BTL air freight unit buys German firm.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Swedish transportation company BTL said on Thursday its air and sea division, the Wilson Group, bought part of  Ballauf Air GmbH, a German air freight company.</p>
<p>&quot;Wilson Group...has acquired operations in Ballauf Air GmbH, an air freight company with special competence in international logistics solutions including for the garment industry and ship spares,&quot; BTL said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Wilson Group has subsidiaries in 16 countries. Its net turnover in 1996 totalled 3.7 billion crowns, BTL said.</p>
<p>Ballauf Air, started in 1988, has a turnover of about 25 million marks annually and is based in Hamburg, it said.</p>
<p>-- Abigail Schmelz, Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1003</p>
